  "faq_heading": "Richmond schools: your questions answered",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The BC Ministry of Education and Child Care school list shows 69 schools with a Richmond street address: 53 public schools and 16 independent schools. It also shows 4 college and university campuses. In that list, 10 schools marked as offering French Immersion, 2 Francophone schools run by the Conseil scolaire francophone, 2 alternate programs and 3 online schools."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public schools here are run by School District 38 (Richmond) and School District 93 (Conseil scolaire francophone). Count by district: School District 38 (Richmond): 51, School District 93 (Conseil scolaire francophone): 2."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Alternate programs, continuing education centres and online schools that have a street address sit under \"other public schools and programs\"; the level of every school is read from its name."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public secondary schools with a Richmond address: A.R. MacNeill Secondary, Cambie Secondary, Hugh Boyd Secondary, Hugh McRoberts Secondary, J.N. Burnett Secondary, Matthew McNair Secondary, R C Palmer Secondary and Richmond Secondary and 2 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Ministry file marks these Richmond schools as offering French Immersion: Alfred B Dixon Elementary, Henry Anderson Elementary, Hugh McRoberts Secondary, James Gilmore Elementary, James Whiteside Elementary, John G Diefenbaker Elementary, Mitchell Elementary, Robert A. McMath Secondary, Tomekichi Homma Elementary and William Bridge Elementary."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Independent schools listed for Richmond include Ark Elementary Montessori Reggio School, Az-Zahraa Islamic Academy, BC Muslim School, Canada Star Secondary School, Chaoyin Bilingual School and Choice School For Gifted Children and 10 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Before an offer, ask the district which school serves the exact street address."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Richmond school district publishes its catchments only as an interactive map, not as a list of streets. Use the district's own page to check an address:",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Richmond school district catchments and school finder",
      "h": "https://sd38.bc.ca/schools/locations-catchments/",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Conseil scolaire francophone publishes its attendance zones (zones de fréquentation) on its own site:",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
